From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:08:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Play full screen with the map and status on the touch screen

The top screen shows the game at its own resolution, the touch screen
always shows the status bar, the map and the weapons.

- The top screen shows the middle 256x192 of the 320x200 frame 1:1. The
  view fills it at high detail. Doom's 320x200 had pixels 1.2 times
  taller than wide on a 4:3 monitor, so on the square pixels of the DS
  the vertical projection is 1.2 times the horizontal one
  (R_PIXELASPECT): walls, sprites, the weapon, floors and the sky keep
  their proportions with the same 90 degree field of view, without
  cropping or stretching. Walls are lit by their horizontal scale, like
  sprites.
- Menus, messages, the intermission stats and the finale texts are drawn
  1:1 inside the visible part, moved where they were outside it. Finale
  texts, HUD and menu messages wrap at words where they are wider, the
  three menu items wider than it are squeezed.
- Frames with a picture made for the whole screen (title, credits, the
  intermission maps, end pictures) set v_fullscreenpicture and are
  scaled to the top screen by the affine background hardware instead,
  smoothed by the half pixel offset layer. The mode and palette change
  with the page flip.
- A view taller than the space above the status bar has no status bar
  or border, the screen around it is black, also when a wipe or scaled
  frame shows all of it.
- The touch screen shows the classic status bar, the automap with the
  level name, time, kills, items and secrets, and 2 rows of stone cells:
  the weapons with their pickup pictures (the fist and pistol as held,
  scaled down), slot numbers and ammo, which select them when tapped,
  and the status bar's ammo table. The map is redrawn every other
  frame, Doom runs at 35 tics a second. Outside of a level it shows the
  logo and the controls, like with the settings open. Dragging the
  stylus no longer turns and SELECT no longer shows the whole
  map, the map always follows the player.
